From m_olshansky at yahoo.com  Fri Aug 17 04:21:05 2007
From: m_olshansky at yahoo.com (Moshe Olshansky)
Date: Thu, 16 Aug 2007 19:21:05 -0700 (PDT)
Subject: [BioC] [R] function to find coodinates in an array
In-Reply-To: <380-22007841674051531@ochoa.fib.es>
Message-ID: <144131.71218.qm@web32201.mail.mud.yahoo.com>

A not very good solution is as below:

If your array's dimensions were KxMxN and the "linear"
index is i then
n <- ceiling(i/(K*M))
i1 <- i - (n-1)*(K*M)
m <- ceiling(i1/K)
k <- i1 - (m-1)*K

and your index is (k,m,n)

I am almost sure that there is a function in R which
does this (it exists in Matlab).

Regards,

Moshe.

